{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant plus a motion-command plant, then layer compact specifications that map sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one safe recovery action and otherwise bias exploration toward random_walk with periodic short forward pulses. Action states self-loop on path_clear so intended one-shot commands are not preempted, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion in plant automata.",
    "Use one policy specification for exploration/recovery and one alternation specification to avoid long forward streaks by requiring random_walk before the next move_forward."
  ],
